# ~/.config/secrets/env — Machine-local secrets, sourced by shell init on every session.
#
# SETUP (required on every machine, unless using the sops-nix alternative below):
#   1. mkdir -p ~/.config/secrets
#   2. Create ~/.config/secrets/env with the export lines below (copy this
#      file if you have nix-atelier cloned locally; otherwise just write it
#      by hand, it's a plain shell file)
#   3. Fill in your values
#
# This file is for secrets that cannot be committed to any repo. Any
# program (Claude Code, Copilot, CLI tools, scripts) can read these by
# sourcing this file, which this repo's shell init does on every session.
# Nothing here is required by this framework itself — none of these
# variables gate any feature in modules/features/*.nix. Add whatever your
# own tools actually need; the two below are illustrative only. If more
# than one of your own repos wants a shared secrets file, point them all at
# this same path instead of keeping separate copies.
#
# DO NOT commit ~/.config/secrets/env — it is gitignored globally by Nix.
#
# Alternative: sops-nix (opt-in, off unless your flake.nix's lib.mkConfigs
# call sets atelier.sops.file via extraConfig — see templates/default/flake.nix
# and modules/secrets-sops.nix). If enabled, these same vars are decrypted
# from your own secrets.yaml straight to this same path, and this manual
# copy-and-fill step isn't needed.

# GitHub personal access token (Settings -> Developer settings -> Personal access tokens)
export GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=""

# Whatever else your own tools need, following the same pattern:
export MY_SERVICE_PAT=""
